# WHICH LICENCE APPLIES TO WHICH FILE, AS DATA. Read by check-licensing.sh.
#
# Open Source Licensing Decision 001 remains the unchanged historical Accepted Source.
# The owner's direct decision on 2026-10-29 supersedes only its hardware licence variant with
# CERN-OHL-S-2.0. LICENSING.md expresses the current policy: firmware and software tools
# GPL-3.0-only, hardware design files CERN-OHL-S-2.0, documentation CC-BY-4.0, brand assets all
# rights reserved. This file says which actual paths fall where, so the gate enforces a recorded
# decision instead of a guess.
#
# ⛔ WHY EVERY EXCEPTION CARRIES A REASON. A gate that only knows "this file lacks our header"
# creates pressure to add our header to files that must never carry it — a vendored typeface, an
# upstream licence text, a serial capture that is evidence, a file whose parser would break. Each
# `except` line below therefore states WHY, and the gate prints that reason. If a future
# contributor is tempted to silence this gate by re-headering third-party material, the reason is
# the answer, and it is in the same place as the rule.
#
# FORMAT — one rule per line, fields separated by `|`, FIRST MATCH WINS.
#
#   require | <glob> | <SPDX id>   the file must carry that identifier AND our copyright line
#   foreign | <glob> | <SPDX id>   we generate and commit it, but its licence is not ours: that
#                                  identifier and an upstream copyright notice are required, and
#                                  our copyright line is FORBIDDEN
#   except  | <glob> | <reason>    the file is deliberately not project-headered
#
# Globs are shell patterns matched against the repository-relative path, and `*` crosses `/`.
# Order matters: put the narrow rules above the broad ones.
#
# A tracked file matching NO rule is an error, not a pass. That is deliberate: new third-party
# material, a new file type or a new area cannot enter the tree without someone deciding here
# which licence it carries.

# --- Generated from Inter: OFL, not ours ------------------------------------
#
# The seven generated LVGL faces are a Modified Version of Inter 4.1 under the OFL, decided by the
# owner on the evidence: the OFL's own definition of "Modified Version" covers derivatives made
# "by changing formats or by porting the Font Software to a new environment", and the pipeline in
# generate-fonts.py does that three ways over — it substitutes cmap entries to freeze `tnum`,
# subsets the glyph set, and rasterises TTF outlines into LVGL C arrays. OFL clause 5 then binds:
# the Font Software "modified or unmodified, in part or in whole, must be distributed entirely
# under this license, and must not be distributed under any other license." SIL's FAQ 1.3 draws
# the boundary that keeps the firmware unaffected: "Only the portions based on the Font Software
# are required to be released under the OFL."
#
# `-no-RFN` is the precise identifier because Inter 4.1 declares no Reserved Font Name, verified
# against the vendored licence text in assets/fonts/inter/PROVENANCE.md rather than assumed.
#
# `foreign`, not `except`: these files are generated and committed by this project, so their
# headers must stay correct — and `require` would have demanded our copyright line on material
# licensed to someone else.
foreign | firmware/components/ui/src/fonts/prd_font_*.c | OFL-1.1-no-RFN

# --- Third-party material — never re-headered as project-owned ---------------
except | assets/fonts/inter/*.ttf | vendored Inter 4.1 typeface, OFL-1.1, (c) Inter Project Authors
except | assets/fonts/inter/LICENSE.txt | upstream OFL-1.1 text, copied unmodified
except | firmware/managed_components/* | third-party components fetched at build time; not tracked

# --- Licence texts — they ARE the licence ------------------------------------
#
# CC-BY-4.0's own terms forbid modifying the licence text, and the same applies in spirit to the
# other two: a licence with our header inserted is no longer the licence it claims to be.
except | LICENSE | GNU GPL v3 text, verbatim
except | LICENSE-hardware | CERN-OHL-S-2.0 text, verbatim
except | LICENSE-documentation | CC-BY-4.0 text, verbatim

# --- Evidence — a header would alter the record ------------------------------
except | hardware/validation/evidence/*.log | verbatim serial capture; evidence must not be edited
except | firmware/test/fixtures/*.json | captured printer response; byte-exact or it proves nothing

# --- Files whose parser cannot take a comment -------------------------------
except | firmware/version.txt | read whole by file(READ)+STRIP; a new line joins the version
except | firmware/test/render/preserved-pixels.txt | machine-parsed name/tick/digest rows; a comment header breaks verify.py and alters preserved evidence
require | firmware/test/render/operational-pixels.txt | GPL-3.0-only
except | firmware/.idf-version | single-value marker, content fixed by Bootstrap Spec 3.3
except | firmware/dependencies.lock | generated; Bootstrap 5.1 forbids editing it

# --- Under hardware/, but documentation by content ---------------------------
#
# Classified by reading them, not by the directory they sit in. Neither is hardware design
# material. waveshare-esp32-s3-lcd-2.8.md is a validation RECORD of a board this project did not
# design: our measurements, decisions, defects and reasoning. It cites the vendor schematic by URL
# and SHA-256 and says it is deliberately not redistributed, so there is no design here from which
# hardware could be made, and nothing for CERN-OHL-S-2.0's reciprocity to attach to.
# evidence/README.md is a ten-line note on the naming and redaction convention for the directory.
#
# Neither is evidence itself — the 15 serial captures are, and they stay untouched below.
#
# ⬅️ NOTE FOR A FUTURE READER. LICENSING.md lists hardware/ among the CERN-OHL-S-2.0 paths,
# beside four CAD directories. That row anticipates design files; the directory holds none yet.
# When real design files arrive they take the hardware licence, and they need their own rule here.
require | hardware/validation/*.md | CC-BY-4.0
require | hardware/validation/evidence/README.md | CC-BY-4.0
require | firmware/test/fixtures/*/README.md | CC-BY-4.0
require | firmware/test/ota-adapter/README.md | CC-BY-4.0

